<link href="/css/product-info-description.css?v=" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css">
    <div class="product-accordion">

        <!-- Content -->
        <div class="panel-group" id="accordion" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true">

            <div class="panel panel-default">
                <div class="panel-heading active" role="tab" id="productDetailsHeading">
                    <h4 class="panel-title">
                        <a role="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordion" href="#productDetails" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="productDetails">
                            Product Details
                        </a>
                    </h4>
                </div>
                <div id="productDetails" class="panel-collapse collapse in show" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="productDetailsHeading">
                    <div class="panel-body">
                        
                        <div class="rich-text-content">
                            <p class="p1">&nbsp;</p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">The CDSX&reg; Security Master File provides comprehensive and timely details on CDSX-eligible securities, through a database of current securities and a daily / weekly / monthly file of updates. The&nbsp;</span>Fixed Income Terms and Conditions product can be purchased with the security master file.</p>
<p class="p1">&nbsp;</p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">Coverage includes:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Common and preferred shares</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Corporate, federal, provincial and municipal bonds</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Canada savings bonds and premium bonds</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Treasury bills</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Bankers' acceptances</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Commercial paper</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Rights, warrants, units</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Strip bonds and coupon receipts</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Mortgage- and other asset-backed securities</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Exchange-traded options</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Index-linked notes</span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Installment receipts</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">Provides preliminary and confirmed information on securities issues in the form of a database (called the 7030 file) of electronic text files of securities information, including: </span></p>
<ul>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Reference Information such as ISIN, security type, instrument type, market symbol or ticker, alternate security code (e.g. CUSIP), security description, issuer code, maturity date, etc. </span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Features relating to corporate action entitlement events such as interest/dividend payment distribution frequency, currency, interest compounding method, feature start and expiry dates, etc. </span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Restriction indicators for deposit and withdrawals, trade reporting and settlement. </span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">Custodian information such as location and type of custody. </span></li>
<li class="p1"><span class="s1">An update file (called the 7031 file) is sent daily to subscribers with updates and additions to the CDSX Security Master File.</span></li>
</ul>
<h4><span class="s1">Delivery Format</span></h4>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">Frequency: Daily / Weekly / Monthly</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">Format: Fixed length text (.txt) made up of six record types</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1">Delivery: FTP</span></p>                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

